      "body": "  ## Motivation\n\n  Fixes #44145.\n\n  `EagleDraftWorker` loads its own `embed_tokens`/`lm_head`, but only binds them\n  to the target's tensors in `alloc_memory_pool()`. The scheduler sizes the target\n  KV pool in `init_target_memory_pool()` before that, so the duplicate draft\n  tensors are still resident during profiling and the KV pool is permanently\n  undersized.\n\n  ## Modifications\n\n  - Call an idempotent `_share_embed_and_head()` at the end of\n    `EagleDraftWorker.__init__`, before the scheduler profiles free memory.\n  - `alloc_memory_pool()` reuses that state instead of calling\n    `init_token_map()` / `init_lm_head()` again.\n\n  ## Verification\n\n  RTX 4090, Qwen3.5-2B, `--speculative-algorithm NEXTN`:\n\n  | Config | max_total_num_tokens |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | no speculation | 1,315,939 |\n  | MTP, before | 1,193,623 |\n  | MTP, after | 1,276,396 |\n\n  Greedy output and `spec_accept_length` are unchanged.\n\n  New CPU regression test:\n  `test/registered/unit/spec/test_eagle_share_embed_and_head.py` — 2 passed.\n\n  ## Note\n\n  This fixes the KV sizing order. It does not reduce peak memory while the draft\n  model itself is being constructed; on a 24 GB GPU a 27B untied-embedding model\n  can still need more memory than is available before the sharing point.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #39236327175](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39236327175)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #39236327334](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39236327334)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #39236327150](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39236327150)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
